 "result": "The session cookie uses a tagging serializer that wraps non-JSON types in a one-key dict marker on save and unwraps it on load.\n\n**Session side: `src/tessel/sessions.py`**\n- `SignedCookieSessionInterface` (L284) sets `serializer = session_json_serializer` (L300), which is a module-level `TypedCookieSerializer()` (L273).\n- It hands the serializer to itsdangerous's `URLSafeTimedSerializer` (L316), which signs and encodes the cookie.\n\n**Tagging side: `src/tessel/json/tag.py`**\n- `TypedCookieSerializer` (L219) keeps an ordered list of tag classes. Its main methods:\n  - `tag()` (L289): the first tag whose `check()` matches converts the value with `to_json()`.\n  - `untag()` (L297): looks up the tag key in a one-key dict and calls `to_python()`.\n  - `dumps()` (L321) and `loads()` (L325): the JSON entry points.\n  - `register()` (L256): adds custom tags.\n- `TypeMarker` (L60) is the base class. Each subclass defines `key`, `check`, `to_json` and `to_python`.\n- The types you asked about:\n  - `TagTuple` (L133): the tuple becomes a list on the way out, and `to_python` turns it back into a tuple.\n  - `TagBytes` (L159): base64-encoded string.\n  - `TagDateTime` (L205): HTTP-date string, parsed back to a `datetime`.\n- Other tags:\n  - `TagDict` (L93) escapes user dicts that look like a tag.\n  - `PassDict` (L119) and `PassList` (L147) recurse into containers.\n  - `TagMarkup` (L173) handles `Markup`.\n  - `TagUUID` (L191) handles `UUID`.",
